Not all component data was extracted. Only the substrate. However, when selecting "multiple outputs" I got the remaining compounds. 

SMILE code not in paper, and the model found a wrong one. For cyclohex-2-en-1-ol instead of cyclohexene oxide.

Only one concentration was extracted for Cyclohexene oxide, despite the concentration changed in reactions.
Same for solubility data, only one data point extracted - same for enzyme concentration.
- For one of the components (Ethyl acetate), the model did add it twice, but not for all components. 

For purity for chemicals and the enzyme the extracted value is 0, but nothing is mentioned in the paper

Added hydrogen as Hydrogen (carrier gas for GC), but this is a part of the autosampler, and not a component added. 
Paper reads: "Chiral GC analysis was performed on a GC-6890N gas chromatograph
(Agilent, Stevens Creek Blvd, Santa Clara, CA 95051)
equipped with an CP7502 column (Agilent, Stevens Creek Blvd,
Santa Clara, CA 95051) equipped with CTC Analytics HTC PAL
Autosampler System and FID detection using hydrogen as carrier
gas. The testing samples were prepared by diluting the ethyl
acetate extracts to 0–7 mM. All samples were analyzed by the
program as follow: 90°C–200°C in 22 min, hold 13.3 min."